Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 05.T06

- [ ] **05.T06.** Add explicit Orbit/Fly/Walk controls, target-based zoom/dolly and bounded adjustable movement speed in one scene. Preserve pose/selection across supported switches. Implement the bounded query-based Walk controller and ready support neighborhood required to traverse the street/doorway/interior; missing support, streamed replacement and changed-source penetration stop/reconcile visibly. General rigid/flexible simulation stays in stages [18](../contracts/Rigid-and-articulated-physics-contracts.lingua)–[19](../contracts/Continuum-and-thermal-contracts.lingua) and is not inferred from this controller.

### Task 05.T07

- [ ] **05.T07.** Make mounted content visible/readable/interactive as its projection grows through the existing surface/input/focus adapters. Faraway content uses bounded representations/markers; native render targets, media streams and detailed colliders need explicit demand. Show the same ball/Sand/object IDs in spatial, numeric and flat views, without geography-specific save/undo/selection implementations.

